W: 2. She gathered up her lovely flowers
W: And spent her time in sport,
W: As if in pretty Cupid's bowers
W: She daily did resort.
W:
W: (Chorus:)
W: And sing blow away the morning dew
W: The dew and the dew
W: Blow away the morning dew
W: How sweet the winds do blow.
W:
W: 3. The yellow cowslip by the brim,
W: The daffodil as well,
W: The timid primrose, pale and trim,
W: The pretty snow-drop bell.
W: (Chorus:)
W:
W: 4. She's gone with all those flowers sweet
W: Of white, of red, of blue,
W: And unto me, about my feet,
W: Is only left the rue.
W: (Chorus:)
